  "steps": [
    "A diphthong is two vowel sounds that glide together in one syllable.",
    "OI and OY say /oy/ — like in coin and boy.",
    "OU and OW say /ow/ — like in house and cow.",
    "Tip: OI and OU usually go in the middle of words; OY and OW often go at the end!"
  ],
